SU2_RETURN_CURRENT_FACTOR maximum_level=30 maximum_prefix=12 parameters=49 rows=2646 coefficients=56154 negatives=18982 last_exit_negatives=19695 minimum=-877150853588508608701996 witness=(30,14,12,11,25) last_exit_minimum=-591668264510872390407724 last_exit_witness=(30,14,12,11,25) result=FAIL_COEFFICIENTWISE

INTERPRETATION
Let F(z)=sum_r f_r z^r and, for fixed n,t, let

  P_(n,t)(z)
   =sum_(s=0)^t binom(n-1,2s)
      {f_(2s)z^(2s)-f_(2s+1)z^(2s+1)}.

The coefficientwise proposals F(z)P_(n,t)(z)>=0 and
F(z)^2P_(n,t)(z)>=0 are both false.  The first would have combined
with the nonnegative last-exit factor in G(z)=F(z)E(z) to prove the
endpoint current.  Thus the valid last-exit decomposition does not
remove the necessary cross-degree payment.

